    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2ed89a37-0c53-54d0-bfa6-df3438d854e0",
      ":question/problem": "Find $m$, if $2{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $m$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}+m\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the second components, we get\n\n$$\n-2m=8\\,⟹\\,m=-4.\n$$\n\nBut then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $m$ such that $2{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=0.$",
